{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe current-main macOS census attributes 250.81 worker-phase seconds to external analyzer/grounding tests, with individual phases up to 15.62s. Multiple modules launch real OpenGrep, ast-grep, gitleaks, and metric scans. Reusing immutable scan results or retaining one real boundary per behavior could reduce repeated tool startup and traversal, but the evidence is not yet sufficient to remove or mock any real boundary.\n\nTracker guard: shockproof-twill-porpoise proves tool presence/absence and explicit coverage accounting are contractual. crushable-choosable-llama retains real scanner/process integration. OSS practice is mixed: pip and pytest reuse expensive session fixtures, while Semgrep retains real CLI snapshot E2E tests marked kinda_slow. No automatic OSS-consensus approval exists yet.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory every >=1s analyzer node, the exact binary invocation, fixture tree, detector/backend, and unique failure mode.\n- Build a fault-seeded equivalence matrix for discovery, rule loading, timeout, invalid output, tool absent, tool present, SARIF/evidence normalization, and consumer fail-open/fail-closed behavior.\n- Measure candidates that share immutable fixture trees or scan results while retaining at least one real invocation for each external boundary and environment state.\n- Compare matched before/after timings and retained failure-mode detection with maintained OSS examples.\n- Recommend implement/keep only after every removed invocation has equivalent behavioral and contractual detection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every affected real-tool invocation maps to a unique failure mode; checked against collected node IDs, subprocess call sites, fixtures, and CI workflow selectors.\n- [ ] Every affected real-tool invocation maps to a faster overlapping oracle when one exists; checked in the fault-seeded equivalence matrix.\n- [ ] Tool-present behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Tool-absent behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Timeout behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Invalid-output behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Rule-discovery behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Evidence-accounting behavior remains explicit; checked against the current test and subprocess contract.\n- [ ] Each reachable failure class has an exact-defect seed and a current detecting oracle recorded in the matrix.\n- [ ] Each proposed retained set has an exact-defect detecting oracle recorded for every reachable failure class.\n- [ ] Matched macOS wall-time savings are measured with repeated pytest runs of the same collected nodes.\n- [ ] Aggregate runner savings are calculated from the matched measurements and current CI matrix.\n- [ ] Ticket-history evidence is cited by ticket alias.\n- [ ] At least three maintained OSS projects are cited with exact repository paths or URLs and the comparable practice.\n- [ ] No production code or test files change; checked with `git diff --exit-code`.\n- [ ] No scanner invocation is removed or mocked.\n\n## Verification\n- Collect the relevant node set with `pytest --collect-only -q` plus repository search of subprocess and backend call sites.\n- Run matched selected-node timing samples with `pytest -vv --durations=0` using the worktree virtualenv.\n- Run existing focused tests that exercise each fault class and record exact node outcomes in the matrix.\n- Confirm the research worktree remains unchanged with `git status --short` and `git diff --exit-code`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786910262996472001,"uuid":"88a9c0ba-448d-42ab-a04d-30728069ecfa"}